{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfs4RD9aGAaPkpg4G4vrT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Both bugs are fixed in `sched/core.py`, and the signature is unchanged. `tests/test_sched.py` passes (2 passed). I didn't commit anything.\n\n**Root causes**\n\n1. **Wrong \"today\" (the skipped-day bug).** `today = now.date()` used the UTC date instead of the date in `tz`. The code then added only one day, so it could return a time that is still at or before `now`. Your example: 23:30 UTC on June 1 (19:30 EDT) is already June 2 in Berlin, but the old code took June 1, produced June 2 01:00 Berlin (23:00 UTC), and that is before `now`.\n2. **\"Next day\" done in UTC (the DST bug).** `candidate + timedelta(days=1)` was computed in UTC, so the local wall-clock time shifted by an hour when the offset changed. For example, 08:00 on March 28 in Berlin, plus 24 hours in UTC, landed on 09:00 CEST on March 29 instead of 08:00.\n\n**Fix**\n\n- `now` is normalized to UTC, so the comparison is between instants.\n- \"Today\" is the calendar date in `tz`.\n- The function builds today's candidate in `tz`. If that is not after `now`, it builds tomorrow's candidate by calendar date in `tz`. Both candidates use `tzinfo=zone`, so the wall-clock time is preserved across DST.\n\n**Tests**\n\n- I added `test_keeps_wall_clock_time_across_dst_change` (Berlin, March 28 to March 29, 2026, expects 08:00 CEST). This is a regression test for the DST bug. I reasoned through the old code's output for it but did not run the old code against the new test.\n- I added a `ZoneInfo` import to the test file for that test.\n- `python -m pytest -q tests/test_sched.py`: 2 passed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":15454,"cache_read_input_tokens":32037,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":15454},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"af9c75e4-2be4-43b8-8c29-5e3cb4e185c3","uuid":"2dced47c-0b35-4cb3-90ae-a851f4242e6d","timestamp":"2026-10-09T17:30:02.545Z","request_id":"req_011Cfs4RCtTGFUVFapKMyGB6"}
